<title>INDIA: INDIA HINDUSTAN LEVER H1 1996 NET HIGHER.</title>
<headline>INDIA HINDUSTAN LEVER H1 1996 NET HIGHER.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    1,213.9 vs   1,055.4</p>
<p>    Net sales	    22,092.7 vs  16,100.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Hindustan Lever Ltd (HLL) -- a unit of Unilever NV/Plc</p>
<p>-- said the current year figures were not</p>
<p>comparable to the previous year as this year's results included</p>
<p>the operations of the detergents business carried on behalf of</p>
<p>Hind Lever Chemicals Ltd. HLL said the turnover and costs of the</p>
<p>bulk chemicals and fertiliser businesses were not reflected in</p>
<p>the above results as they had been hived off to Hind Lever Chem.</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	   6.0 vs	N.A.</p>
<p>    Other income	    321.4 vs     247.4</p>
<p>    Expenditure	  19,750.5 vs  14,403.0</p>
<p>    Gross Profit	  2,552.9 vs   1,863.9</p>
<p>    Interest costs	  110.7 vs	80.5</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    167.6 vs     119.4</p>
<p>    Tax			 906.4 vs     689.1</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items   265.0 vs     --</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom + 91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
